# Messages that contain a count need the right noun form: "1 page", not
# "1 pages". The TRANSLATIONS value is the general form ("other", and for
# Arabic also "many"); only the forms that differ are listed here. The
# Russian messages are phrased "Label: {count}", which needs no inflection,
# and Japanese, Chinese and Korean have no plural forms. Arabic "one" and
# "two" forms name the number in words, so they carry no {count}.
